A||||6||Eric||Building my own exhaust||||1||
Z||000000||Eric||03-09-2001||10:53 AM||||Since I'm probably going to drop the cradle anyway when I do a suspension overhaul, I think I'll replace the old exhaust system too.  I'm going with a single 2.5 in/ single 2.5 out 40 series Flowmaster.  I'm going to leave out the cat for now and substitute a 2.5" pipe.  The exaust will follow the same route as the original.  What I need is to find a source for 2.5" diameter pipe and 2.5" mandrel bends along with a reducer to go from just below the flange that meets the ypipe to rest of the exhaust down stream.  All the parts will be welded together.||||reg||1
Z||000001||GoCartGuy||03-09-2001||10:59 AM||||Just remember one thing Eric, without the cat you won't pass emissions testing.  If its not required where you live it cool, just don't move.  The previous owner did a similar set up on mine, I priced around on having a cat reinstalled and since it was all welded, I was told by three different places that I'd have to replace the entire exhaust assembly.  Best price I was quoted was $900 for the whole fix.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||03-09-2001||11:12 AM||||Here in FL I passed my last two smog insp without cat with no problem. They even had the little mirror to look under. No more smog test in FL since last June. I wonder why...<BR>Replacing the whole system just for a cat? That's pure BS from the shop. They just want your money. Any welder can install just the cat back.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||03-09-2001||01:05 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.brullenexhaust.com" TARGET=_blank>www.brullenexhaust.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.jegs.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jegs.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.summitracing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.summitracing.com</A>  all have manrel bend tubing.. from 1" -5"||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eric||03-09-2001||01:49 PM||||Oh, okay, I didn't even consider Jegs or Summit.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||03-09-2001||01:51 PM||||Don't rebuild the whole exhaust for a missing cat, heck, Rodney's got a setup to replace one on stock size piping, or if it's not a standard size, a little cutting and welding and you can have a new cat in for the price of the parts.||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||03-09-2001||02:34 PM||||Have to replace the WHOLE exhaust for the cat because its welded???<P>Exhaust shops have these funny little things called torches that WELD AS WELL AS CUT! When a cat goes bad do they always replace the WHOLE EXHAUST???<P>DUDE! Thats a LOAD of crap!!!!!<BR>STAY THE HELL AWAY FROM THAT PLACE!!!!<P>Any reputable exhaust place will just cut the old cat (or straight pipe) and reweld a new one on. <P>Even when I had my 2.5 inch mandrel bent exhaust (cat back) custom made it didn't cost me more than $300 in California!<P>Though going back to your original thread make sure you have enough space where the exhaust goes past the motor mount...don't want to toast it!<P>||||reg||8
